{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":287406,"duration_api_ms":287354,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge in observable behavior. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components:\n- `cmd/` — per-utility Go binaries with differential tests\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (runs Go vs GNU binary, compares stdout/stderr/exit)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions (terminal, stat, signals)\n- `pkg/format/` — shared formatting (columns, human-readable sizes)\n- `magefiles/` — build targets (scaffolded, not a generation target)\n\n**Current implementation** (from source_code): `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, and `cmd/wc` all exist with working code. No source code exists for `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`, or any other utility on this branch.\n\n**Current release priority**: rel01.1 (cat) is the earliest incomplete release with complete specs. rel00.0 and rel01.0 are effectively complete (all code-generatable packages exist). rel01.2 (sponge), rel01.3 (du) have complete specs but depend on rel01.1 completing first. rel02.0+ specs are still pending.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is **rel01.1 — cat**. Specs are complete (PRD, use case, test suite all exist). Code status is \"not started\". Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks. Per P8, implementation comes before tests. Therefore the next task is implementing `cmd/cat/main.go`.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/cat: file concatenation and output transformation (cat PRD)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/ (list this directory; find and read the PRD for cat, named prdNNN-cat.yaml)\"\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml (cat use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.1.yaml (cat test suite)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component, design decisions DD1-DD7)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (reference implementation pattern for cmd/ utilities)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"cat utility: flag parsing, file concatenation, output transformations\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement file concatenation per the cat PRD: read named files in argument order, read stdin when no files are given, and treat '-' as explicit stdin. Write all content to stdout.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Parse all flags defined in the cat PRD using manual GNU-style argument parsing (no flag package). Support combined short flags (e.g. -vET), long flags (e.g. --show-all, --number, --number-nonblank, --show-ends, --show-tabs, --show-nonprinting, --squeeze-blank), and the '--' end-of-options delimiter. Follow the parseArgs pattern established in cmd/wc/main.go.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement all output transformations defined in the cat PRD: line numbering (-n/--number, -b/--number-nonblank), show line ends (-E/--show-ends appends '$'), show tabs (-T/--show-tabs displays as ^I), show non-printing characters (-v/--show-nonprinting using caret and M- notation), squeeze consecutive blank lines (-s/--squeeze-blank), and composite flags (-A/--show-all equivalent to -vET, -e equivalent to -vE, -t equivalent to -vT). All under LC_ALL=C semantics.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Handle exit codes and errors per the cat PRD: exit 0 on success, exit 1 if any file cannot be opened or read. Report errors to stderr in the format 'cat: <path>: <error message>' and continue processing remaining files. Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at program start.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the cmd/wc implementation pattern: define a config struct for parsed flags, implement parseArgs() with manual GNU-style argument parsing, use bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout) for buffered output, and call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at program start.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Process output byte-by-byte to support position-dependent transformations (line numbering at line start, end-of-line markers, non-printing character expansion). Track start-of-line state and consecutive blank line count across buffer reads.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Target LC_ALL=C semantics per ARCHITECTURE design decision DD6. Under LC_ALL=C, one byte equals one character. Non-printing character display uses caret notation (^X for 0x00-0x1F, ^? for 0x7F) and M- notation (M-^X for 0x80-0x9F, M-x for 0xA0-0xFE, M-^? for 0xFF), matching GNU cat.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/cat/main.go compiles successfully with 'go build ./cmd/cat/' with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All flags defined in the cat PRD are parsed correctly, including combined short flags (-vET), long flags (--show-all), and the '--' end-of-options delimiter.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Output transformations produce correct output: -n numbers all lines starting at 1, -b numbers only non-blank lines, -E appends '$' at each line end, -T displays tabs as ^I, -v displays non-printing bytes in ^X/M- notation, -s collapses consecutive blank lines to one, and composite flags -A/-e/-t expand to their component flags.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Error handling matches GNU cat: nonexistent files produce 'cat: <file>: No such file or directory' on stderr, exit code is 1 when any file fails, and remaining files continue processing after an error.\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"d3d